  "paper_diagnosis": "Severe Dengue Fever with Haemolytic Anaemia",
  "disease_label_per_paper": "Severe dengue fever complicated by immune hemolytic anemia",
  "expected_manifold": "D-DENGUE",
  "demographics": {
    "age": 22,
    "sex": "M"
  },
  "presentation_summary": [
    "22-year-old Sri Lankan man presented with 3 days of high-grade intermittent fever associated with chills, rigors, vomiting, and loose stools.",
    "Dengue NS1 antigen and dengue IgM were positive at diagnosis; later serology showed dengue IgM and IgG positivity.",
    "He initially denied abdominal pain, myalgia, retro-orbital pain, and back pain, but developed bleeding manifestations during the critical phase.",
    "On illness day 5 he developed venipuncture-site hematomas and gingival bleeding with platelet nadir 14 x10^9/L and stable hematocrit 45-46%.",
    "Ultrasound showed bilateral basal pleural effusions, ascites, and hepatitis, indicating plasma leakage and hepatic involvement.",
    "On illness day 8-9 he developed hemolytic anemia with hemoglobin fall to 8.4-8.5 g/dL, reticulocytosis, indirect hyperbilirubinemia, high LDH, and positive indirect Coombs test.",
    "He was treated with carefully titrated isotonic crystalloid and monitoring, then recovered and was discharged with normal hemoglobin, white blood cells, and platelets."
  ],
